---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Cycle from '../components/Cycle.astro';
import { DISCLOSURES } from '../data/site.ts';
const title = "Sozoris - Break it. Prove it. Make it whole.";
const description = "Sozoris is a security firm that attacks what you built the way a real adversary would, proves exactly how it breaks, and stays until every finding is closed and retested - VAPT, red teaming, threat hunting, OSINT and attack surface analysis.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
<div class="scene">
<section class="back dark">
  <div class="hero-bg" aria-hidden="true"><span class="glow"></span><span class="scan"></span></div>
  <div class="wrap hero-grid">
    <div>
      <Cycle class="greek" />
      <h1>We break what you built.<br>Then we <span class="r">make it whole.</span></h1>
      <p class="sub">Sozoris is a security firm built on one conviction: finding the weakness is the easy half. We attack your systems the way a real adversary would, prove exactly how they give, and stay until every finding is closed and retested.</p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span> Every finding proven with a working exploit - no scanner noise, no theoretical risk</li>
        <li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span> Fixes your engineers can act on, evidence your board can read</li>
        <li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span> Free retest of every remediated finding - the engagement ends when it holds</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="row"><a href="contact.html" class="btn btn-fill">Book a free consultation <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a><a href="services.html" class="btn btn-out">Explore services</a></div>
    </div>
    <form class="formcard" onsubmit="return false">
      <h2>Talk to our team</h2><div class="fsub">Tell us about your environment and we will scope an assessment.</div>
      <div class="two"><div><label>First name*</label><input placeholder="First name" /></div><div><label>Last name*</label><input placeholder="Last name" /></div></div>
      <label>Work email*</label><input type="email" placeholder="you@company.com" />
      <label>Message</label><textarea placeholder="What would you like tested?"></textarea>
      <button class="btn" type="submit">Send message</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sheet light cutA"><div class="geo" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="wrap"><div class="why"><span class="eyebrow">Break it. Prove it. Make it whole.</span>
    <h2>Finding the hole is the easy part.</h2>
    <p>Anyone can hand you a list of vulnerabilities. We measure ourselves on what is still open the day we leave - so every engagement runs through to a proven fix, not a PDF.</p>
    <div class="cols"><div class="item"><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span> Exploit-proven, manual penetration testing</div><div class="item"><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span> Every finding reproduced before it is reported</div><div class="item"><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span> Remediation guidance, not just a severity label</div><div class="item"><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span> Free retest until the fix is proven to hold</div><div class="item"><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span> Findings ranked by business impact, not CVSS alone</div><div class="item"><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span> Evidence packaged for your auditors and regulators</div></div></div><div class="logowall"><div class="lwlabel">Research by our team has found &amp; disclosed vulnerabilities in</div><div class="logorow"><img src="assets/logos/better-auth.png" alt="Better Auth" title="Better Auth - OAuth refresh-token replay (Critical) &amp; OIDC crypto defaults (High)" loading="lazy" /><img src="assets/logos/n8n.svg" alt="n8n" title="n8n - OAuth authorization bypass (CVE-2026-33720)" loading="lazy" /><img src="assets/logos/sap.svg" alt="SAP" title="SAP - @sap/hdi-deploy SQL injection, vendor-validated + bounty" loading="lazy" /><img src="assets/logos/twilio.svg" alt="Twilio" title="Twilio - validated finding, HackerOne bounty (CVSS 6.5)" loading="lazy" /><img src="assets/logos/fusionauth.svg" alt="FusionAuth" title="FusionAuth - trusted researcher, private program" loading="lazy" /></div></div>
  </div>
</section>
</div>
<section class="hsv" id="services"><div class="hsv-head"><span class="eyebrow">What we do</span><h2>Attack it first. Then make it hold.</h2><p>Manual, exploit-driven engagements run by people who compromise systems for a living - across web, API, network, cloud and your people. Every one of them ends in a verified fix.</p></div><div class="hsv-track"><div class="hsv-stage"><div class="hsv-left"><div class="hsv-sheet cA" data-i="0" style="transform:translateY(0)"><div class="hsv-num">01</div><div class="eyebrow">Step 01 &middot; VAPT</div><h3>Penetration Testing (VAPT)</h3><p>Manual, exploit-driven testing - and a retest that proves the fix.</p></div><div class="hsv-sheet cB" data-i="1" style="transform:translateY(110%)"><div class="hsv-num">02</div><div class="eyebrow">Step 02 &middot; Red Teaming</div><h3>Red Teaming</h3><p>Find out whether your defences hold against a real adversary.</p></div><div class="hsv-sheet cC" data-i="2" style="transform:translateY(110%)"><div class="hsv-num">03</div><div class="eyebrow">Step 03 &middot; Threat Hunting</div><h3>Threat Hunting</h3><p>Find whoever is already inside, and close the way they came in.</p></div><div class="hsv-sheet cA" data-i="3" style="transform:translateY(110%)"><div class="hsv-num">04</div><div class="eyebrow">Step 04 &middot; OSINT</div><h3>OSINT &amp; Exposure</h3><p>Everything an adversary can learn for free, taken back off the table.</p></div><div class="hsv-sheet cB" data-i="4" style="transform:translateY(110%)"><div class="hsv-num">05</div><div class="eyebrow">Step 05 &middot; ASM</div><h3>Attack Surface Analysis</h3><p>A continuously accurate map of everything you are responsible for.</p></div></div><div class="hsv-right"><div class="hsv-pane active" data-i="0"><div class="eyebrow">VAPT</div><span class="hsv-ic"><Icon name="vapt" /></span><h4>Penetration Testing (VAPT)</h4><p>Find what is genuinely exploitable, then prove it closed.</p><ul><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Every finding proven with a working exploit</li><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Web, API, network, cloud &amp; mobile coverage</li><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Free retest within the engagement window</li></ul><a class="lm" href="service-vapt.html">Explore VAPT <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></div><div class="hsv-pane" data-i="1"><div class="eyebrow">Red Teaming</div><span class="hsv-ic"><Icon name="red-team" /></span><h4>Red Teaming</h4><p>Test whether your defences actually hold under pressure.</p><ul><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Intelligence-led, scenario-driven operations</li><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Full narrative mapped to MITRE ATT&amp;CK</li><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Purple-team replay to tune your detections</li></ul><a class="lm" href="service-red-teaming.html">Explore Red Teaming <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></div><div class="hsv-pane" data-i="2"><div class="eyebrow">Threat Hunting</div><span class="hsv-ic"><Icon name="threat-hunting" /></span><h4>Threat Hunting</h4><p>Find what is already inside, and evict it for good.</p><ul><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Hunts across endpoint, identity &amp; network</li><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Confirmed compromise fully scoped</li><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>New detections left running behind us</li></ul><a class="lm" href="service-threat-hunting.html">Explore Threat Hunting <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></div><div class="hsv-pane" data-i="3"><div class="eyebrow">OSINT</div><span class="hsv-ic"><Icon name="osint" /></span><h4>OSINT &amp; Exposure</h4><p>Close what you are leaking into the open.</p><ul><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Shadow IT &amp; forgotten infrastructure</li><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Leaked credentials &amp; secrets</li><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Prioritized takedown &amp; rotation plan</li></ul><a class="lm" href="service-osint.html">Explore OSINT <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></div><div class="hsv-pane" data-i="4"><div class="eyebrow">ASM</div><span class="hsv-ic"><Icon name="attack-surface" /></span><h4>Attack Surface Analysis</h4><p>Know every asset you are actually responsible for.</p><ul><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Attributed inventory of all assets</li><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Change tracking over time</li><li><span class="ck"><Icon name="check" /></span>Risk-ranked, exploitable exposures</li></ul><a class="lm" href="service-attack-surface-analysis.html">Explore ASM <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></div></div><div class="hsv-hint" aria-hidden="true"><span class="hsv-dot"></span><span class="hsv-dot"></span><span class="hsv-dot"></span><span class="hsv-dot"></span><span class="hsv-dot"></span></div></div></div></section>
<div class="scene">
<section class="back dark">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="shead"><span class="eyebrow">Verified research</span><h2>Proof you can check yourself.</h2><p>We would rather show you findings a vendor has publicly confirmed than testimonials you have no way to verify. Every entry below is externally checkable.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sheet light cutB"><div class="geo" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="stats three"><div class="stat"><div class="v"><span class="num" data-to="5">0</span></div><div class="l">Vendors with accepted disclosures</div></div><div class="stat"><div class="v"><span class="num" data-to="1">0</span></div><div class="l">CVE assigned to our research</div></div><div class="stat"><div class="v"><span class="num" data-to="2">0</span></div><div class="l">Bug bounties awarded</div></div></div>
    <div class="ledger">{DISCLOSURES.map((d) => (
      <div class="lrow">
        <span class="lv"><img src={d.logo} alt="" loading="lazy" />{d.vendor}</span>
        <span class="lf">{d.finding}{d.cve ? <> &middot; <code>{d.cve}</code></> : null}</span>
        <span class="ls">{d.status}</span>
      </div>
    ))}</div>
    <div style="text-align:center;margin-top:clamp(28px,4vh,44px)"><a href="case-studies.html" class="btn btn-out">Read case studies <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></div>
  </div>
</section>
</div>
<div class="scene">
<section class="back dark" id="insights">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="shead"><span class="eyebrow">Resources</span><h2>Explore our latest insights.</h2></div>
    <div class="posts"><a class="post" href="insight-why-most-zero-days-start-as-forgotten-assets.html"><div class="thumb"><span class="cat">Attack Surface</span></div><div class="pb"><div class="meta">12 May 2026 &middot; 6 min read</div><h3>Why most zero-days start as forgotten assets</h3><p>The dangerous part of an unknown asset is not that it is vulnerable. It is that no one is watching it long enough to notice when it becomes a problem.</p></div></a><a class="post" href="insight-red-team-vs-penetration-test-choosing-the-right-engagement.html"><div class="thumb"><span class="cat">Engagements</span></div><div class="pb"><div class="meta">3 Apr 2026 &middot; 7 min read</div><h3>Red team vs penetration test: choosing the right engagement</h3><p>They are not the same service at different price points. They answer different questions, and buying the wrong one wastes a real opportunity.</p></div></a><a class="post" href="insight-the-economics-of-an-attack-path.html"><div class="thumb"><span class="cat">Strategy</span></div><div class="pb"><div class="meta">18 Feb 2026 &middot; 6 min read</div><h3>The economics of an attack path</h3><p>Attackers are rational actors with budgets. Understanding their cost model tells you which defenses actually change their behavior.</p></div></a></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sheet light cutC ctajaws"><span class="jaw jaw-l" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="jaw jaw-r" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="geo" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="wrap cta-in"><span class="eyebrow">Make it whole</span><h2>Ready to find out what actually <span class="r">holds?</span></h2><p>Book a scoped assessment. We will map what is reachable, prove what is exploitable, and stay with you until every finding is closed and retested.</p><a href="contact.html" class="btn btn-fill">Book a free scoping call <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></div>
</section>
</div>
</Base>
